id: jf-snok
title: Add typed OpenAPI invocation contracts for agents
description: "Enrich exact Jellyfin OpenAPI operation inspection with parameter types, formats, constraints, defaults, examples, request-body schemas, response contracts, security requirements, and deterministic executable CLI templates so agents can construct valid requests without guessing or mutating the live server during discovery."
type: Plan
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[7]: agents,api,contracts,openapi,read-only,schemas,typescript
created_at: "2026-07-31T20:20:37.363Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T20:58:10.157Z"
assignee: codex-jellyfin-contracts
author: codex-jellyfin-contracts
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "jf api inspect exposes deterministic parameter schema metadata, request bodies, responses, security requirements, and a ready-to-fill jf api get or mutate argv template; All nested help and TOON, JSON, YAML, Markdown, table, and raw outputs remain valid and documented; Implementation is fully typed, uses top-level imports and erasable syntax, preserves the 300-code-line rule, and reads external contracts rather than guessing; Focused tests, full release validation, generated changelog parity, strict PM validation, and compiled live read-only acceptance pass without persisting private data"
definition_of_ready: All-status PM lineage and duplicate search are complete; Jellyfin 10.11.11 is confirmed latest stable; local main is refreshed; owner-only global profile exists.
goal: jf-mqpo
value: Give humans and LLM agents enough machine-readable contract detail to invoke every OpenAPI operation correctly on the first attempt.
impact: Reduces invalid requests and dangerous guesswork while making the generic all-API executor genuinely usable in automated workflows.
outcome: "Exact Jellyfin operation inspection becomes a complete, deterministic invocation contract rather than a shallow name list."
why_now: "The live coverage report maps all 429 operations, but current exact inspection omits the schemas and response/security details agents need to use that coverage safely."
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: github-review-bots
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-10.11.11
release: next-manual-release
